{"type":"message","id":"1212530a","parentId":"9c8b6a76","timestamp":"2026-05-18T08:20:14.885Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — here’s the exact problem statement.\n\n## Problem statement\n\nThe pipeline is **functionally completing**, but the **writer stage is unstable because agent output is being captured through a terminal stream that includes spinner/control-sequence noise**.\n\n### What I’m facing inside the pipeline\n\n1. **Research step works**\n   - Research agent returns usable JSON.\n   - No blocker there.\n\n2. **Writer step is the core failure point**\n   - When I run the writer and redirect output into `/tmp/crypto-article.md`, the captured file can include:\n     - terminal spinner text like `Waiting for agent reply…`\n     - ANSI escape/control characters\n     - mixed transport noise before the real article\n   - This corrupts the article file and breaks downstream validation.\n\n3. **Writer obeys badly on compression passes**\n   - When asked to shorten an oversized article, it sometimes does the opposite:\n     - first pass produced ~6081 words\n     - compression pass still produced ~3283 words\n     - another tightening pass expanded to ~6287 words\n   - So the summarization/recovery logic is not reliable.\n\n4. **File-cleaning recovery is fragile**\n   - Because the captured output is noisy and inconsistently structured, cleanup logic can fail.\n   - One cleanup attempt removed the whole file because the expected marker was not stable.\n\n5. **Non-interactive capture helped**\n   - Re-running the writer in a cleaner/non-PTY path produced a usable article:\n     - final clean article was ~1203 words\n     - Word Count block present\n   - So the pipeline can succeed, but the capture method is brittle.\n\n---\n\n## Root issue in one line\n\n**The pipeline’s main failure is unreliable writer-output capture and cleanup, especially when `openclaw agent --deliver` output is redirected to a file and terminal/progress noise gets mixed into the article.**\n\n---\n\n## Symptoms I observed\n\n- Spinner/progress text leaked into `/tmp/crypto-article.md`\n- ANSI terminal garbage polluted the article file\n- compression prompts made drafts longer instead of shorter\n- cleanup logic was not deterministic\n- downstream steps only worked after a cleaner regeneration path\n\n---\n\n## What likely needs fixing\n\n### Primary fix\nMake writer output capture **structured and noise-free**:\n- either force truly non-interactive/plain output from `openclaw agent --deliver`\n- or provide a machine-readable mode like JSON/raw/final-only output\n- or suppress spinner/progress UI when stdout is redirected\n\n### Secondary fix\nStrengthen writer control:\n- enforce hard max word limit\n- reject drafts >1500 before returning\n- make “summarize to 1100–1200” deterministic\n\n### Tertiary fix\nImprove validation/capture boundary:\n- write only the assistant’s final content to file\n- do not include transport/progress/status lines in redirected stdout\n\n---\n\n## Short version you can use for debugging\n\n**Pipeline bug:** Writer-stage output capture is contaminated by terminal spinner/progress text and ANSI control sequences when redirected to `/tmp/crypto-article.md`. Recovery summarization is also unreliable, sometimes expanding the article instead of shrinking it. Result: article generation is unstable even though the broader pipeline can still complete with a clean non-interactive rerun.\n\nIf you want, I can also give you:\n1. a **1-paragraph bug report**  \n2. a **repro command sequence**  \n3. a **suggested fix spec** for OpenClaw output handling."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":2276,"output":717,"cacheRead":40192,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":43185,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779092401263,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DgnUjRg3FE761H1huprEPIStvHoB3"}}
