w agent --agent creator --message \"Generate a feature image for this article. Title: 'CLARITY Act lifts Bitcoin to $79,084 as sentiment jumps'. Topic: CLARITY Act Advances as Bitcoin and Crypto Markets React to U.S. Regulatory Momentum. Key Facts: CoinDesk reported that the Senate Banking Committee voted to advance the CLARITY Act to a full Senate vote after a bipartisan committee checkpoint.; Decrypt reported that Senators Ruben Gallego and Angela Alsobrooks voted for the bill despite ethics concerns tied to President Trump’s personal crypto ventures, while all Republican committee members also supported it. Crypto Asset: Bitcoin. Use the Scene Formula in your SOUL.md to pick the rig\n\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-0502.md#L17-L27","source":"memory","citation":"memory/2026-05-18-0502.md#L17-L27","corpus":"memory"},{"id":"69c60178251811099c785bd05558e0e0465d751f4fc567f235c3818fbd59d360","path":"memory/2026-05-18-0502.md","startLine":1,"endLine":21,"score":1,"textScore":0.3861347167404448,"snippet":"# Session: 2026-05-18 05:02:05 UTC\n\n- **Session Key**: agent:orchestrator:telegram:direct:5691449303\n- **Session ID**: 10f45462-5d8c-41cc-8988-8fd90369afce\n- **Source**: telegram\n\n## Conversation Summary\n\nassistant: [[reply_to_current]] ✅ Article written, generating chart...\nassistant: [[reply_to_current]] ✅ Chart generated, generating feature image...\nassistant: [[reply_to_current]] I’ve finished the chart step and I’m at feature image generation now.\n\nPlease approve this exact command in the Web UI or terminal UI so I can continue:\n\n```bash\nrm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/creator/sessions/sessions.json\nopenclaw agent --agent creator --message \"Generate a feature image for this article. Title: 'CL\n\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-0502.md#L1-L21","source":"memory","citation":"memory/2026-05-18-0502.md#L1-L21","corpus":"memory"},{"id":"8125dc5a5b01b5ff585f5e48395ad389f00354ed7a8c73311b7981a3b2803ed5","path":"memory/2026-05-18-0510.md","startLine":98,"endLine":105,"score":1,"textScore":0.5859856829731631,"snippet":"openclaw agent --agent creator --message \"Generate a feature image for this article. Title: 'CLARITY Act lifts Bitcoin to $79,084 as sentiment jumps'. Topic: CLARITY Act Advances as Bitcoin and Crypto Markets React to U.S. Regulatory Momentum. Key Facts: CoinDesk reported that the Senate Banking Committee voted to advance the CLARITY Act to a full Senate vote after a bipartisan committee checkpoint.; Decrypt reported that Senators Ruben Gallego and Angela Alsobrooks voted for the bill despite ethics concerns tied to President Trump’s personal crypto ventures, while all Republican committe\n...[truncated]...\n```\nEND_QUOTED_NOTES\n\nA new session was started via /new or /reset. Execute your Sessi\n\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-0510.md#L98-L105","source":"memory","citation":"memory/2026-05-18-0510.md#L98-L105","corpus":"memory"}],"provider":"none","citations":"auto","debug":{"backend":"builtin","effectiveMode":"n/a","searchMs":15,"hits":10}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779093136958}}
{"type":"message","id":"d78f05b7","parentId":"6cbbb7a1","timestamp":"2026-05-18T08:33:35.635Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Absolutely — here’s the **full, all-in-one, developer-facing reliability report** for the crypto news pipeline.\n\nI’m **not changing anything**. This is a specification, diagnosis, and blueprint only.\n\n---\n\n# Crypto News Pipeline: Full Reliability, Stability, and Hardening Report\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis document explains:\n- **every important failure point**\n- **why the pipeline feels brittle**\n- **what specific fixes should be made**\n- **how to redesign the pipeline so it becomes stable, resumable, and predictable**\n- **what validations and contracts each step should use**\n- **what the developer should implement first**\n\nThis report assumes the current pipeline flow is:\n\n1. Research\n2. Write\n3. Generate chart\n4. Generate feature image\n5. Publish to Google Drive\n6. Ask for confirmation\n7. Publish to WordPress draft\n\n---\n\n# 1. Executive summary\n\nThe pipeline’s biggest problem is not one single bug. It is that the system relies too heavily on:\n\n- **freeform agent output**\n- **implicit assumptions between steps**\n- **temporary files with shared names**\n- **text parsing instead of contracts**\n- **weak validation before proceeding**\n- **retries that are prompt-based instead of failure-type-based**\n\nThe pipeline can complete, but it is **fragile by design**.\n\n## In one sentence:\nThe pipeline needs to move from **chat-style orchestration** to **contract-driven orchestration**.\n\nThat means:\n- every agent returns structured output\n- every step validates success before proceeding\n- every artifact is explicitly tracked\n- every retry is targeted\n- every run has isolated files\n- every published result is verified\n\n---\n\n# 2. What happened in the observed runs\n\nFrom the recent runs, these real issues showed up:\n\n## 2.1 Writer output corruption\nThe writer stage captured terminal/progress noise such as:\n- spinner text\n- “Waiting for agent reply…”\n- control/ANSI sequences\n\nThat contaminated the article file itself.\n\n### Result\n- article markdown became polluted\n- cleanup logic became unreliable\n- validation was confused\n- article regeneration had to be repeated\n\n---\n\n## 2.2 Compression passes were nondeterministic\nWhen the article was too long:\n- initial draft was ~6081 words\n- summarization pass still returned ~3283 words\n- next “tightening” pass expanded to ~6287 words\n\n### Result\nThe retry logic did not stabilize the step. It amplified unreliability.\n\n---\n\n## 2.3 Cleanup logic was brittle\nA cleanup attempt tried to strip noisy transport output based on a marker, but the marker was inconsistent.\n\n### Result\nThe file was effectively blanked / invalidated.\n\n---\n\n## 2.4 Chart generation succeeded, but handoff clarity was weak\nThe chart file existed, but there was confusion about whether the chart was properly embedded into the WordPress post.\n\n### Result\nThere was ambiguity around whether:\n- the placeholder remained\n- the wp-publisher handled it\n- the rendered draft was correct\n\nEven when the final result turned out okay, the **pipeline did not prove it cleanly**.\n\n---\n\n## 2.5 WordPress publish result was under-verified\nA URL came back, but there was no strong verification that:\n- the draft was correct\n- chart placeholders were replaced\n- feature image was attached\n- rendered content matched expectations\n\n### Result\nThe user had to manually inspect reality.\n\n---\n\n## 2.6 Duplicate / awkward user-facing messaging happened\nAt least one reply duplicated content or combined status messages awkwardly.\n\n### Result\nThe orchestration layer was not fully controlling message state.\n\n---\n\n## 2.7 Manual approval / async continuation path is fragile\nOn Telegram, long-running commands and approvals can interrupt clean continuity.\n\n### Result\nThe system often needs:\n- external approval\n- manual “continue”\n- resumed state inference\n\nThis is manageable, but only if step state is strictly persisted.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Core architectural problem\n\nThe pipeline is currently designed as though agent outputs are trustworthy human-readable responses that can be safely interpreted.\n\nThat does not scale well.\n\n## Current pattern\n- run command\n- capture text\n- infer meaning\n- extract pieces\n- continue optimistically\n\n## Reliable pattern\n- run command\n- receive strict result object\n- validate schema\n- validate artifact\n- store run state\n- proceed only if validated\n\n---\n\n# 4. Full pipeline failure map\n\nBelow is a step-by-step breakdown of all likely weak points.\n\n---\n\n# 5. Step 1 — Research\n\n## Current purpose\nFind the biggest news story and produce a structured data summary.\n\n## Failure risks\n1. Output not valid JSON\n2. Missing fields required later\n3. Too many stories mixed together\n4. Weak extraction of primary asset / chart coin\n5. Source URLs missing or low quality\n6. Inconsistent field naming\n7. Hidden commentary before/after JSON\n8. Researcher returns narrative instead of schema\n9. Poor confidence in topic selection\n10. Upstream RSS variability\n\n## What should be fixed\nResearcher must return **JSON only**, no prose outside it.\n\n## Recommended required schema\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"story_id\": \"2026-05-18-hormuz-bitcoin\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Iran may be turning the Strait of Hormuz into a bitcoin-based insurance market, local reports say\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Iran mulls a Bitcoin-paid insurance or toll scheme for ships transiting the Strait of Hormuz\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Hormuz Bitcoin\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"Bitcoin\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"bitcoin\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.84,\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://...\",\n    \"https://...\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"...\",\n    \"...\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\n## Required validation\nBefore continuing:\n- JSON parses successfully\n- required keys exist\n- `source_urls.length >= 2`\n- `combined_key_facts.length >= 3`\n- `chart_coin` non-empty\n- `primary_asset` non-empty\n- confidence above threshold or flagged\n\n## Retry logic\nIf invalid:\n- retry once with “return valid JSON only”\n- if still invalid, stop pipeline and report `[blocked: research output invalid]`\n\n---\n\n# 6. Step 2 — Writer\n\n## Current purpose\nTurn research JSON into a complete crypto article following the template.\n\n## This is the most failure-prone step.\n\n## Observed failures\n- output capture contaminated by spinner/progress text\n- word count exploded\n- compression retries were unreliable\n- cleanup logic was fragile\n- output format was not deterministic\n\n## Failure risks\n1. PTY / interactive output pollutes file\n2. writer includes thinking blocks\n3. writer includes commentary before article\n4. word count too short\n5. word count too long\n6. section structure wrong\n7. missing Sources block\n8. missing Word Count block\n9. malformed markdown\n10. wrong placeholders\n11. title line missing\n12. inconsistent metadata block\n13. repeated content\n14. hallucinated structure\n15. recovery prompts make draft worse\n\n## Root cause\nThe writer is treated like a conversational agent instead of a deterministic renderer.\n\n## Recommended design\nThe writer should return one of two things only:\n- **strict markdown article**\nor\n- **strict JSON wrapper with article content field**\n\nBest option:\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"title\": \"Hormuz Bitcoin plan targets $10B in Strait transit revenue\",\n  \"word_count\": 1184,\n  \"chart_placeholders\": 2,\n  \"article_markdown\": \"META\\n...\\n# Title\\n...\"\n}\n```\n\nIf keeping plain markdown output, then it must be:\n- non-interactive\n- no PTY\n- no spinner\n- no “thinking”\n- no commentary\n- article only\n\n## Required validation after writing\nValidate:\n- starts with expected metadata or title\n- exactly one H1 title\n- Sources section exists\n- Word Count block exists\n- total word count is between configured bounds\n- placeholder count matches expectation\n- no ANSI/control characters\n- no “Waiting for agent reply”\n- no `<thinking>` blocks\n- no duplicated sections\n\n## Word count strategy\nCurrent behavior is too loose.\n\n### Better pattern\n- writer has hard target: 1100–1200\n- accepted range: 1000–1300\n- warning range: 1301–1500\n- fail range: >1500 or <900\n\n## Retry strategy\nDo not endlessly “summarize” by prompt alone.\n\nUse failure-type-based repair:\n- if noisy output → rerun in clean mode\n- if too long → run dedicated compression pass with explicit max word target\n- if missing block → run structure repair pass\n- if malformed markdown → run normalization pass\n- if second attempt still invalid → stop and mark failed\n\n## Absolute recommendation\n**Writer output must never be captured from a PTY stream if file cleanliness matters.**\n\n---\n\n# 7. Step 2.5 — Chart generation\n\n## Current purpose\nGenerate price chart based on `chart_coin`.\n\n## Failure risks\n1. chart file missing\n2. wrong coin chart\n3. wrong time range\n4. chart generator returns plain text, not contract\n5. file exists but corrupt\n6. chart path stale from previous run\n7. chart generated but publish layer does not use it\n\n## Recommended output contract\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"bitcoin\",\n  \"days\": 30,\n  \"output_path\": \"/tmp/.../chart.png\",\n  \"mime\": \"image/png\",\n  \"width\": 1600,\n  \"height\": 900\n}\n```\n\n## Required validation\n- file exists\n- file type is png\n- non-zero size\n- dimensions are sane\n- `chart_coin` matches research result\n- article placeholder count known\n\n## Additional recommendation\nRecord expected placeholder count at writer step so chart insertion later can verify exact replacement count.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Step 3 — Feature image generation\n\n## Current purpose\nGenerate article hero image.\n\n## Failure risks\n1. returned path but file absent\n2. wrong file type\n3. stale previous image reused\n4. commentary mixed with result\n5. oversized or broken image\n6. failure path ambiguous\n\n## Recommended output contract\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"output_path\": \"/tmp/.../crypto-feature.jpg\",\n  \"mime\": \"image/jpeg\",\n  \"width\": 1024,\n  \"height\": 576\n}\n```\n\nIf failed:\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"error\",\n  \"code\": \"IMAGE_FAILED\",\n  \"message\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\n## Required validation\n- file exists\n- correct mime\n- non-zero size\n- current-run artifact, not stale\n- dimensions acceptable\n\n---\n\n# 9. Step 4 — DOCX / Google Drive publishing\n\n## Current purpose\nPrepare export artifact and upload to Google Drive.\n\n## Current weak points\n- artifact composition is partly implicit\n- output extraction from publisher is plain text\n- no full contract around upload result\n- docx validity not always explicitly checked\n\n## Failure risks\n1. docx not created\n2. docx created from wrong source\n3. feature image inserted but chart logic inconsistent\n4. upload returns noisy output\n5. link extraction fails\n6. wrong Google account\n7. uploader says success but no valid URL returned\n\n## Recommended output contract from publisher\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"file_name\": \"Crypto News - 2026-05-18\",\n  \"file_id\": \"abc123\",\n  \"webViewLink\": \"https://docs.google.com/document/d/...\",\n  \"mime\": \"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document\"\n}\n```\n\n## Required validation\nBefore upload:\n- docx exists\n- docx non-zero size\n- source article path known\n- feature image decision known\n\nAfter upload:\n- valid `webViewLink`\n- upload file id present\n- correct account used\n- file name matches current date\n\n---\n\n# 10. Step 5 — Confirmation gate\n\n## Current purpose\nPause after Google Drive publish and ask whether to publish to WordPress.\n\n## Risks\n1. reported URL might be hallucinated if upstream weak\n2. article title may not match uploaded doc\n3. state not persisted across pause\n4. “yes/no” resume may not know exact current run state\n5. another pipeline run may overwrite temp artifacts before confirmation\n\n## Recommendation\nAt this point, the system must persist a **run manifest**.\n\nExample:\n```json\n{\n  \"run_id\": \"2026-05-18T08-06-12Z\",\n  \"status\": \"awaiting_wordpress_confirmation\",\n  \"article_title\": \"...\",\n  \"research_path\": \"...\",\n  \"article_path\": \"...\",\n  \"chart_path\": \"...\",\n  \"feature_image_path\": \"...\",\n  \"docx_path\": \"...\",\n  \"google_doc_url\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\nWithout this, resume is fragile.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Step 6 — WordPress draft publishing\n\n## Current purpose\nPublish article + image (and chart handling) to WordPress draft.\n\n## This is the second major fragility zone.\n\n## Failure risks\n1. placeholder format mismatch\n2. wp-publisher ignores chart placeholders\n3. chart uploaded but not inserted\n4. feature image uploaded but chart not\n5. returned URL valid but content incomplete\n6. post created in wrong status\n7. no replacement-count reporting\n8. no rendered verification\n9. different permalink shapes confuse validation\n10. old temp file paths break upload\n\n## Recommended output contract\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"post_id\": 91,\n  \"draft_url\": \"https://example.com/?p=91\",\n  \"feature_image_uploaded\": true,\n  \"chart_uploaded\": true,\n  \"chart_placeholders_found\": 2,\n  \"chart_placeholders_replaced\": 2,\n  \"post_status\": \"draft\"\n}\n```\n\nIf failed:\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"error\",\n  \"code\": \"WP_FAILED\",\n  \"message\": \"chart upload failed\",\n  \"partial\": {\n    \"post_created\": true,\n    \"post_id\": 91\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Required validation\nBefore publish:\n- article file exists\n- feature image exists or failure acknowledged\n- chart file exists if placeholders expected\n- placeholder count known\n\nAfter publish:\n- post id present\n- draft url present\n- replacements count equals found count\n- rendered content smoke check passes\n\n---\n\n# 12. Rendered post smoke test\n\nThis is one of the most important missing pieces.\n\nAfter WordPress draft creation, the system should verify:\n- title appears\n- article body appears\n- feature image appears\n- chart appears at least once\n- raw placeholders do not appear\n- local `/tmp/...` paths do not appear in rendered HTML\n\n## Why this matters\nA publish step is not done when a URL exists.  \nIt is done when the **rendered page is correct**.\n\n---\n\n# 13. Temp file strategy is a major hidden weakness\n\n## Current pattern\nShared temp names like:\n- `/tmp/crypto-article.md`\n- `/tmp/chart.png`\n- `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg`\n\n## Risk\nThese can be:\n- overwritten by later runs\n- mistakenly reused from old runs\n- referenced after a delay\n- confused across resumptions\n\n## Recommended fix\nUse a per-run directory.\n\nExample:\n```text\n/tmp/crypto-pipeline/2026-05-18T08-06-12Z/\n  research.json\n  article.md\n  chart.png\n  feature.jpg\n  article.docx\n  manifest.json\n```\n\n## Benefits\n- no stale collisions\n- easy debug\n- easy resume\n- easy cleanup\n- easy handoff tracking\n\nThis one improvement alone would reduce a lot of confusion.\n\n---\n\n# 14. Run manifest is essential\n\nA `manifest.json` should be updated after each successful step.\n\n## Example\n```json\n{\n  \"run_id\": \"2026-05-18T08-06-12Z\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-05-18T08:06:12Z\",\n  \"status\": \"wordpress_published\",\n  \"step\": \"wp_publish\",\n  \"story\": {\n    \"title\": \"Hormuz Bitcoin plan targets $10B in Strait transit revenue\",\n    \"primary_asset\": \"Bitcoin\",\n    \"chart_coin\": \"bitcoin\"\n  },\n  \"artifacts\": {\n    \"research_json\": \"/tmp/crypto-pipeline/.../research.json\",\n    \"article_markdown\": \"/tmp/crypto-pipeline/.../article.md\",\n    \"chart_png\": \"/tmp/crypto-pipeline/.../chart.png\",\n    \"feature_jpg\": \"/tmp/crypto-pipeline/.../feature.jpg\",\n    \"docx\": \"/tmp/crypto-pipeline/.../article.docx\"\n  },\n  \"results\": {\n    \"google_doc_url\": \"https://docs.google.com/...\",\n    \"wordpress_draft_url\": \"https://example.com/?p=91\"\n  },\n  \"checks\": {\n    \"article_word_count\": 1203,\n    \"chart_placeholders_found\": 2,\n    \"chart_placeholders_replaced\": 2\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Why this matters\nThen “continue pipeline” no longer relies on guesswork.\n\n---\n\n# 15. Retry logic should be redesigned\n\n## Current problem\nRetries are mostly prompt variations.\n\nThat is not enough.\n\n## Better model\nRetries should be chosen by **failure class**.\n\n### Failure class → action\n- invalid JSON → JSON repair retry\n- noisy PTY output → rerun non-PTY\n- too-long article → compression retry\n- missing section → structure repair retry\n- missing artifact → rerun specific generator\n- upload success but no URL → result extraction retry\n- publish success but missing chart → rendered content diagnosis\n\n## Retry limits\nEvery step should have:\n- max retries = 1 or 2\n- then fail clearly\n\nInfinite optimism creates hidden failures.\n\n---\n\n# 16. Validation framework by step\n\n## Research validator\nMust check:\n- parsable JSON\n- required keys\n- at least 2 sources\n- chart coin present\n- topic not empty\n\n## Writer validator\nMust check:\n- no ANSI/control sequences\n- no spinner text\n- no `<thinking>`\n- title exists\n- Sources exists\n- Word Count exists\n- word count in range\n- placeholder count valid\n- output size reasonable\n\n## Chart validator\nMust check:\n- file exists\n- PNG type\n- dimensions valid\n- non-zero size\n\n## Feature image validator\nMust check:\n- file exists\n- JPEG/PNG type\n- dimensions valid\n\n## Publish validator\nMust check:\n- docx exists\n- upload returned file id\n- upload returned valid URL\n\n## WordPress validator\nMust check:\n- draft URL returned\n- post id returned\n- placeholder replacement counts returned\n- rendered draft contains no raw placeholder text\n\n---\n\n# 17. Problem with freeform agent output\n\nThe whole system gets unstable when agents return things like:\n- commentary\n- progress text\n- explanations\n- “I’m doing X now”\n- terminal stream updates\n\nThose are okay for humans, bad for orchestration.\n\n## Strong recommendation\nSeparate:\n- **machine result**\nfrom\n- **human logs**\n\nFor example:\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"result\": {...},\n  \"logs\": [\n    \"Fetched data...\",\n    \"Built image...\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nOr return only machine result and keep human commentary out of stdout.\n\n---\n\n# 18. User-facing messaging issues\n\n## Observed risk\nMessages can duplicate, arrive out of order, or include awkward partial progress.\n\n## Why this happens\nThe orchestration layer is reacting both to command completions and its own status updates without a strict messaging rule.\n\n## Recommendation\nUser messages should be emitted only on:\n- confirmed step success\n- meaningful blocker\n- final completion\n- explicit confirmation request\n\nAvoid reporting speculative success.\n\n---\n\n# 19. Async continuation / approval issues\n\n## Current reality\nTelegram/manual approval flow interrupts command continuity.\n\n## Risk\nWhen the user later says “continue,” the orchestrator must infer:\n- what already finished\n- what file is authoritative\n- what still needs to run\n\n## Recommendation\nPersist step state externally in manifest form so `continue pipeline` becomes:\n- load manifest\n- see last completed step\n- validate artifacts\n- continue from next step\n\nWithout that, async resumptions remain brittle.\n\n---\n\n# 20. Definition of done for the entire pipeline\n\nThe pipeline should be considered complete only if:\n\n## After Google Drive stage\n- research valid\n- article valid\n- chart valid\n- feature image valid or intentionally skipped\n- docx valid\n- google doc link valid\n\n## After WordPress stage\n- draft url valid\n- post id valid\n- feature image uploaded\n- chart placeholders handled\n- rendered draft passes smoke test\n\n---\n\n# 21. Full recommended architecture\n\n## Recommended orchestration model\nEach step should output:\n1. status\n2. artifacts\n3. validations\n4. warnings/errors\n\n### Generic step result envelope\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"step\": \"writer\",\n  \"artifacts\": {\n    \"article_markdown\": \"/tmp/.../article.md\"\n  },\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"word_count\": 1203\n  },\n  \"checks\": {\n    \"has_sources\": true,\n    \"has_word_count_block\": true,\n    \"chart_placeholders\": 2\n  },\n  \"warnings\": [],\n  \"errors\": []\n}\n```\n\nThis makes orchestration deterministic.\n\n---\n\n# 22. Full list of recommended fixes\n\n## Critical fixes\n1. **Force non-PTY/plain output for writer**\n2. **Require structured result contracts from all agents**\n3. **Add strict validation after every step**\n4. **Use per-run temp directories**\n5. **Persist a manifest for every run**\n6. **Make wp-publisher report placeholder replacement counts**\n7. **Add rendered WordPress smoke test**\n8. **Do not proceed on invalid step output**\n\n## High-value fixes\n9. **Separate machine output from human commentary**\n10. **Use failure-type-based retries**\n11. **Track artifact freshness**\n12. **Ensure uploader returns file ids, not just links**\n13. **Validate chart/image mime + dimensions**\n14. **Formalize accepted word-count range**\n15. **Guard against stale files**\n\n## Quality-of-life fixes\n16. **Improve user-facing step messages**\n17. **Add run summary report**\n18. **Support step resume explicitly**\n19. **Add per-step timestamps**\n20. **Add warning states distinct from hard failure**\n\n---\n\n# 23. Suggested implementation priority\n\n## Phase 1 — Stop the bleeding\nDo these first:\n1. non-PTY writer output\n2. per-run directory\n3. strict step validators\n4. structured result outputs\n5. manifest file\n\n## Phase 2 — Stabilize publishing\n6. publisher JSON result contract\n7. wp-publisher JSON result contract\n8. placeholder replacement reporting\n9. rendered smoke checks\n\n## Phase 3 — Make it resilient\n10. typed retries\n11. resume from manifest\n12. artifact freshness checks\n13. logs/metrics/run report\n\n---\n\n# 24. Suggested JSON contracts for every agent\n\n## Researcher\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"story_id\": \"string\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"string\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"string\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"string\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"string\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"string\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.0,\n  \"source_urls\": [\"string\"],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\"string\"],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"string\"\n}\n```\n\n## Writer\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"title\": \"string\",\n  \"word_count\": 0,\n  \"chart_placeholders\": 0,\n  \"article_markdown\": \"string\"\n}\n```\n\n## Chart generator\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"string\",\n  \"days\": 30,\n  \"output_path\": \"string\",\n  \"mime\": \"image/png\",\n  \"width\": 0,\n  \"height\": 0\n}\n```\n\n## Creator\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"output_path\": \"string\",\n  \"mime\": \"image/jpeg\",\n  \"width\": 0,\n  \"height\": 0\n}\n```\n\n## Publisher\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"file_name\": \"string\",\n  \"file_id\": \"string\",\n  \"webViewLink\": \"string\"\n}\n```\n\n## WP publisher\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"post_id\": 0,\n  \"draft_url\": \"string\",\n  \"post_status\": \"draft\",\n  \"feature_image_uploaded\": true,\n  \"chart_uploaded\": true,\n  \"chart_placeholders_found\": 0,\n  \"chart_placeholders_replaced\": 0\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n# 25. Suggested validation checklist for developer\n\n## Must validate before next step\n- parseability\n- required fields\n- artifact existence\n- artifact type\n- artifact size > 0\n- no stale-file ambiguity\n- counts and URLs sane\n\n## Must validate before final success\n- Google Doc URL real\n- WordPress draft URL real\n- raw chart placeholders absent from rendered post\n- local temp paths absent from rendered post\n\n---\n\n# 26. Most important philosophy change\n\nThe pipeline currently behaves like:\n> “If the output looks roughly right, continue.”\n\nIt needs to behave like:\n> “If the output is not formally valid, stop.”\n\nThat one philosophy shift will remove a large amount of hidden breakage.\n\n---\n\n# 27. Short diagnosis in plain English\n\nWhy does the pipeline keep feeling like it breaks?\n\nBecause too much of it depends on:\n- interpreting messy text\n- trusting agent behavior\n- hoping retries fix things\n- using shared temp files\n- assuming downstream steps will infer context\n\nThat combination is almost guaranteed to create intermittent failures.\n\n---\n\n# 28. Final recommendation\n\nIf the developer only implements a handful of changes, the **highest impact set** is:\n\n1. **Make every agent return strict structured output**\n2. **Use non-interactive clean output for writer**\n3. **Validate every step before moving on**\n4. **Give each run its own working directory**\n5. **Persist a manifest for resume/debug**\n6. **Require wp-publisher to report placeholder replacement counts**\n7. **Smoke-test the rendered WordPress draft**\n\nIf those are done, the pipeline will become dramatically more reliable.\n\n---\n\n# 29. Bottom line\n\nThe pipeline does not mainly suffer from “bad prompting.”  \nIt suffers from **weak contracts, weak validation, and weak run-state management**.\n\nFix those three, and most of the recurring instability will disappear.\n\n---\n\nIf you want next, I can turn this exact report into either:\n\n1. **a polished engineering memo**\n2. **a shorter developer checklist**\n3. **a ranked impact-vs-effort roadmap**\n4. **a copy-paste spec document your developer can implement directly**\n\nAnd again — I will **not** change anything unless you explicitly ask later."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":60982,"output":5798,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":66780,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779093136960,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DgngcwLV6xzPTQrrvphSYzOCt5ey0"}}
{"type":"message","id":"4e1e4e3a","parentId":"d78f05b7","timestamp":"2026-05-18T08:39:26.679Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"telegram:5691449303\",\n  \"message_id\": \"389\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"5691449303\",\n  \"sender\": \"Sawan bhardwaj\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Mon 2026-05-18 08:39 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Sawan bhardwaj (5691449303)\",\n  \"id\": \"5691449303\",\n  \"name\": \"Sawan bhardwaj\",\n  \"username\": \"hero_fr_fun\"\n}\n```\n\nnow check our developer's plan is it good \"# Definitive Pipeline Hardening Plan\n## Merged: Developer Analysis + Orchestrator Self-Diagnosis\n\n---\n\n## What the Agent Caught That I Didn't\n\nThe agent's self-report adds 4 critical items beyond my original plan:\n\n1. PTY noise contamination — the writer's output file literally contains \"Waiting for agent reply…\" and spinner text mixed into the article markdown. This is a concrete, observed failure that my analysis missed.\n2. Rendered WordPress smoke test — after publishing, actually fetch the live draft URL and verify the HTML contains no local /tmp/ paths and no raw [CHART_PLACEHOLDER] strings. I didn't include this.\n3. Placeholder replacement COUNTS from wp-publisher — the script must explicitly report how many [CHART_PLACEHOLDER] were found and how many were replaced so the orchestrator can verify they match.\n4. Resume from manifest — \"continue pipeline\" should load a persisted manifest and pick up from the last verified step, not rely on the orchestrator's fading context memory.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 — Critical Stability (Do First) ⚡\n\nThese fixes address the root causes of every observed pipeline failure.\n\n### Fix 1: Non-PTY Writer Output (HIGHEST priority)\n\nProblem: The Orchestrator captures writer output with > /tmp/crypto-article.md. The --deliver flag still bleeds PTY noise (\"Waiting for agent reply…\", spinner characters, ANSI codes) into the file. This makes the article file unparseable.\n\n**Fix in workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md Step 2:**\n# Clear writer session\nrm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/writer/sessions/sessions.json\n\n# Run writer in non-interactive mode + immediately strip all noise\nopenclaw agent --agent writer \\\n --message \"Read /tmp/research.json for facts. Write the article following COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md. Output the article ONLY, nothing else.\" \\\n --deliver \\\n --no-color \\\n --no-spinner \\\n 2>/dev/null > /tmp/crypto-article-raw.md\n\n# Strip all PTY noise: thinking blocks, ANSI codes, progress messages\npython3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport re, sys\n\nwith open('/tmp/crypto-article-raw.md', 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\n content = f.read()\n\n# Strip ANSI/control sequences\ncontent = re.sub(r'\\x1b\\[[0-9;]*[mGKHF]', '', content)\ncontent = re.sub(r'\\x1b\\[[0-9;]*[A-Za-z]', '', content)\n\n# Strip thinking blocks\ncontent = re.sub(r'<thinking>.*?</thinking>', '', content, flags=re.DOTALL | re.IGNORECASE)\n\n# Strip PTY progress lines\nnoise_patterns = [\n r'^Waiting for agent reply.*$',\n r'^Sending message.*$',\n r'^\\s*[⠋⠙⠹⠸⠼⠴⠦⠧⠇⠏]\\s.*$', # spinner chars\n r'^\\s*\\.\\.\\.\\s*$',\n]\nfor pattern in noise_patterns:\n content = re.sub(pattern, '', content, flags=re.MULTILINE)\n\n# Clean up excess blank lines\ncontent = re.sub(r'\\n{3,}', '\\n\\n', content).strip()\n\nwith open('/tmp/crypto-article.md', 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n f.write(content + '\\n')\n\nprint(\"Article cleaned and saved to /tmp/crypto-article.md\")\nPYEOF\n\n\n### Fix 2: File-Based Data Handovers\n\nProblem: The Orchestrator passes a 2000+ token JSON blob inside a bash --message \"...\" argument → bash argument quoting breaks the data, destroys context window.\n\n**Fix A — workspace-researcher/SOUL.md:** Add a mandatory bash step BEFORE returning:\n# Save research JSON to the pipeline drop-point\ncat > /tmp/research.json << 'JSON_EOF'\n{paste the JSON here}\nJSON_EOF\necho \"RESEARCH_DONE\"\necho \"CHART_COIN: bitcoin\"\n\nReply to the orchestrator with ONLY 2 lines: RESEARCH_DONE + CHART_COIN: <coin>.\n\n**Fix B — workspace-orchestrator/SOUL.md Steps 1, 2, 3:**\n- Step 1: Stop capturing the JSON blob. Just verify cat /tmp/research.json works.\n- Step 2 (Writer): Message becomes \"Read /tmp/research.json for your research data. Write the article.\" (10 tokens vs 2000).\n- Step 3 (Creator): Message becomes \"Read /tmp/research.json to find the article topic, primary asset, and key facts.\" (safe, no hallucination risk).\n\n### Fix 3: Per-Run Working Directory\n\nProblem: Shared temp files like /tmp/crypto-article.md get contaminated by previous failed runs.\n\nFix in Orchestrator Step 0 (new):\n# Create isolated per-run directory\nRUN_ID=\"$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)\"\nRUN_DIR=\"/tmp/crypto-run-${RUN_ID}\"\nmkdir -p \"$RUN_DIR\"\n\n# Symlink expected static paths (backward-compatible, nothing else needs to change)\nln -sf \"${RUN_DIR}/research.json\" /tmp/research.json\nln -sf \"${RUN_DIR}/crypto-article.md\" /tmp/crypto-article.md\nln -sf \"${RUN_DIR}/chart.png\" /tmp/chart.png\nln -sf \"${RUN_DIR}/crypto-feature.jpg\" /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg\n\necho \"Run ID: $RUN_ID — files isolated in $RUN_DIR\"\n\n\n### Fix 4: Pipeline Manifest (Updated at Every Step)\n\nProblem: \"Continue pipeline\" relies on the orchestrator's fading context memory. After a long pause or a Telegram reconnect, there's no ground truth about what completed.\n\n**Create /tmp/pipeline-manifest.json and update it after each step:**\npython3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json, os\nmanifest = {\n \"run_id\": os.environ.get(\"RUN_ID\"),\n \"last_step\": \"research\", # update per step\n \"story_id\": \"\", # from research.json\n \"primary_headline\": \"\",\n \"chart_coin\": \"\",\n \"artifacts\": {\n \"research_json\": \"/tmp/research.json\",\n \"article_md\": \"/tmp/crypto-article.md\",\n \"chart_png\": \"/tmp/chart.png\",\n \"feature_jpg\": \"/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg\",\n },\n \"checks\": {},\n \"results\": {}\n}\nwith open('/tmp/pipeline-manifest.json', 'w') as f:\n json.dump(manifest, f, indent=2)\nPYEOF\n\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 — Reliability Hardening 🛡️\n\n### Fix 5: Step Validators (After Each Agent)\n\nAfter Step 1 (Research):\npython3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json, sys\ntry:\n with open('/tmp/research.json') as f:\n d = json.load(f)\n required = ['primary_headline','topic_theme','combined_key_facts','source_urls','chart_coin']\n missing = [k for k in required if not d.get(k)]\n if missing:\n print(f\"RESEARCH_INVALID: missing {missing}\")\n sys.exit(1)\n if len(d.get('source_urls', [])) < 1:\n print(\"RESEARCH_INVALID: no source URLs\")\n sys.exit(1)\n print(f\"RESEARCH_VALID: {d['primary_headline'][:60]}\")\nexcept json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n print(f\"RESEARCH_INVALID: JSON parse error: {e}\")\n sys.exit(1)\nPYEOF\n\n→ If validation fails: retry once with \"Return VALID JSON ONLY with no prose outside the JSON block\". If still invalid: stop pipeline.\n\nAfter Step 2 (Writer):\npython3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport re, sys\n\nwith open('/tmp/crypto-article.md', 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n content = f.read()\n\nerrors = []\nwarnings = []\n\n# Hard failures\nif re.search(r'\\x1b\\[', content): errors.append(\"ANSI codes found in article\")\nif 'Waiting for agent reply' in content: errors.append(\"PTY noise in article\")\nif len(content.strip()) < 2000: errors.append(f\"Article too short ({len(content)} chars)\")\n\n# Structure checks\nif not re.search(r'^# .+', content, re.MULTILINE): errors.append(\"No H1 title found\")\nif not re.search(r'sources', content, re.IGNORECASE): warnings.append(\"No Sources section\")\nif not re.search(r'word count', content, re.IGNORECASE): warnings.append(\"No Word Count block\")\n\n# Word count\nwords = len(content.split())\nif words < 900: errors.append(f\"Article too short: {words} words\")\nif words > 1600: warnings.append(f\"Article long: {words} words\")\n\n# Chart placeholders\nph_count = content.count('[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]')\nprint(f\"ARTICLE_STATS: words={words} placeholders={ph_count}\")\n\n# Write placeholder count for wp-publisher to verify later\nwith open('/tmp/expected_placeholders.txt', 'w') as f:\n f.write(str(ph_count))\n\nif errors:\n print(\"ARTICLE_INVALID:\", \"; \".join(errors))\n sys.exit(1)\nif warnings:\n print(\"ARTICLE_WARNINGS:\", \"; \".join(warnings))\n\nprint(\"ARTICLE_VALID\")\nPYEOF\n\n\nAfter Step 2.5 (Chart):\npython3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport subprocess, sys, os\n\nchart = '/tmp/chart.png'\nif not os.path.exists(chart):\n print(\"CHART_MISSING\")\n sys.exit(1)\n\nsize = os.path.getsize(chart)\nif size < 5000:\n print(f\"CHART_SUSPICIOUS: only {size} bytes\")\n sys.exit(1)\n\nresult = subprocess.run(['file', chart], capture_output=True, text=True)\nif 'PNG' not in result.stdout:\n print(f\"CHART_NOT_PNG: {result.stdout}\")\n sys.exit(1)\n\nprint(f\"CHART_VALID: {size} bytes, PNG confirmed\")\nPYEOF\n\n\n### Fix 6: WP-Publisher Reports Placeholder Replacement Counts\n\n**Fix in publish.sh Phase 1.5:** After the Python replacement script, count how many were replaced and write to manifest:\nPLACEHOLDERS_REPLACED=$(python3 -c \"\nimport re\nwith open('${CLEAN_MD}') as f: content = f.read()\n# Count remaining [CHART_PLACEHOLDER] in clean article - should be 0\nremaining = content.count('[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]')\nexpected = int(open('/tmp/expected_placeholders.txt').read().strip()) if os.path.exists('/tmp/expected_placeholders.txt') else 0\nreplaced = expected - remaining\nprint(replaced)\n\")\nlog_info \"Chart placeholders: expected=$EXPECTED_PH found=$PLACEHOLDERS_REPLACED replaced\"\n\n\n**Append to /tmp/wp-result.txt:**\n{\n \"status\": \"ok\",\n \"post_id\": 91,\n \"draft_url\": \"https://...\",\n \"feature_image_uploaded\": true,\n \"chart_uploaded\": true,\n \"chart_placeholders_replaced\": 2\n}\n\n\n### Fix 7: Rendered WordPress Smoke Test (NEW — from Agent Report)\n\nAfter Step 6 (WP-Publisher): The orchestrator fetches the actual rendered WordPress draft and checks:\nDRAFT_URL=$(cat /tmp/wp-result.txt | python3 -c \"import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin).get('draft_url',''))\" 2>/dev/null || cat /tmp/wp-result.txt)\n\npython3 - <<PYEOF\nimport urllib.request, sys\n\nurl = \"${DRAFT_URL}?preview=true\"\ntry:\n with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=15) as r:\n html = r.read().decode('utf-8', errors='ignore')\nexcept Exception as e:\n print(f\"SMOKE_WARN: Could not fetch draft: {e}\")\n sys.exit(0) # non-fatal, continue\n\nissues = []\nif '[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]' in html:\n issues.append(\"Raw chart placeholder still in HTML\")\nif '/tmp/chart.png' in html:\n issues.append(\"Local /tmp path in rendered HTML\")\nif '/tmp/crypto' in html:\n issues.append(\"Local /tmp path in rendered HTML\")\n\nif issues:\n print(\"SMOKE_FAIL:\", \"; \".join(issues))\nelse:\n print(\"SMOKE_PASS: No broken references in rendered draft\")\nPYEOF\n\n\n### Fix 8: Failure-Type-Based Retries\n\nReplace the current generic retry logic with targeted retries:\n\n| Failure | Retry Strategy |\n|---|---|\n| PTY noise in article | Re-run writer with --no-color --no-spinner stricter flags |\n| Article too long | Run dedicated compression pass: \"Compress this article to exactly 1100 words. Keep structure, shorten every paragraph.\" |\n| Article missing Sources | Run structure repair: \"Re-add the Sources section at the end of this article.\" |\n| Research not valid JSON | Retry with \"Return ONLY the JSON object. No prose, no commentary, nothing outside the braces.\" |\n| Chart missing/corrupt | Re-run chart-generator once |\n| WP placeholder mismatch | Log and alert — do not silently continue |\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3 — Production Contracts 📋 (After Phase 1+2 Verified)\n\n### Strict JSON Result Envelopes\n\nEvery agent returns a structured JSON object. The Orchestrator parses it with Python — no text scanning.\n\n| Agent | Final Output |\n|---|---|\n| Researcher | {\"status\":\"ok\",\"story_id\":\"...\",\"chart_coin\":\"bitcoin\",\"research_saved\":\"/tmp/research.json\"} |\n| Writer | {\"status\":\"ok\",\"word_count\":1184,\"chart_placeholders\":2,\"article_path\":\"/tmp/crypto-article.md\"} |\n| Chart-generator | {\"status\":\"ok\",\"output_path\":\"/tmp/chart.png\",\"mime\":\"image/png\",\"chart_coin\":\"bitcoin\"} |\n| Creator | {\"status\":\"ok\",\"output_path\":\"/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg\",\"mime\":\"image/jpeg\"} |\n| Publisher | {\"status\":\"ok\",\"file_id\":\"abc\",\"webViewLink\":\"https://...\"} |\n| WP-Publisher | {\"status\":\"ok\",\"post_id\":91,\"draft_url\":\"https://...\",\"chart_placeholders_replaced\":2} |\n\n### Resume From Manifest\n\nThe Orchestrator's continue pipeline command loads /tmp/pipeline-manifest.json:\nif [ -f /tmp/pipeline-manifest.json ]; then\n LAST_STEP=$(python3 -c \"import json; print(json.load(open('/tmp/pipeline-manifest.json'))['last_step'])\")\n echo \"Resuming from: $LAST_STEP\"\n # Skip already-completed steps\nfi\n\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Order & Summary\n\n| # | Fix | Phase | Files | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Non-PTY writer + noise stripper | 1 | orchestrator SOUL.md | 🔴 Critical |\n| 2 | Researcher saves to file | 1 | researcher SOUL.md |🔴 Critical |\n| 3 | Orchestrator reads files, not blobs | 1 | orchestrator SOUL.md | 🔴 Critical |\n| 4 | Per-run directory | 1 | orchestrator SOUL.md | 🟠 High |\n| 5 | Pipeline manifest | 1 | orchestrator SOUL.md | 🟠 High |\n| 6 | Research validator | 2 | orchestrator SOUL.md | 🟠 High |\n| 7 | Article validator + placeholder count | 2 | orchestrator SOUL.md | 🟠 High |\n| 8 | Chart validator | 2 | orchestrator SOUL.md | 🟡 Medium |\n| 9 | WP placeholder count reporting | 2 | publish.sh | 🟠 High |\n| 10 | Rendered smoke test | 2 | orchestrator SOUL.md | 🟠 High |\n| 11 | Failure-type-based retries | 2 | orchestrator SOUL.md | 🟡 Medium |\n| 12 | Strict JSON contracts all agents | 3 | all SOUL.mds | 🟡 Medium |\n| 13 | Resume from manifest | 3 | orchestrator SOUL.md | 🟡 Medium |\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Phase 1 (fixes 1–5) is the single highest-impact batch. Fixes 1–3 alone will eliminate the majority of observed failures. Do these first and verify before moving to Phase 2.\n\""}],"timestamp":1779093566675}}
